Algorithm 3: Demand Registration and Management

Input:
Owner o, Provider DID d, Resources R, Quantities q, Criticality c

Output:
Demand stored/updated successfully, or transaction reverted with an appropriate error.

Pseudocode
Algorithm 4: Demand Registration and Management

1.  if msg.sender == o then

2.      Register provider using DID d

3.  else
4.      Reject transaction
5.      Error: "Only owner"


6.  if DID d exists then

7.      Generate Demand Number D

8.      For each resource Ri:

9.          Create demand record:
            <D, Ri, qi, ci, NF>

10. else
11.     Reject transaction
12.     Error: "DID not registered"


13. if Demand is updated then

14.     Update resource quantity qi

15.     Update demand timestamp

16.     if qi > 0 then
17.         Set demand status = PF
18.     else
19.         Set demand status = F

20. Return demand matrix:
        (NF, PF)

21. OR return aggregated demand by resource
